{
  "id": "229",
  "title": "How the Chinese Study English",
  "level": "intermediate",
  "date": "2016-12-21",
  "synopsis": "How did Chinese people study English before the invention of tape recorders? A 150 year old English book gives us some insight.",
  "audioUrl": "https://static.duchinese.net/documents/300/d6f1acf7c9bbdd0323075b7cdb0e636047b6ffba.mp3",
  "series": null,
  "fullText": {
    "simplified": "中国人这样学英语\n\n    “托马六、唵以、及夫、尤、唵五史为”，这是什么意思？先别急，读的时候想想英文。是的，这其实是“Tomorrow I give you answer”的发音。\n    这个是150年前英语书上的内容，是给中国人学英语用的。可能是因为那时候没有录音机，人们只能这样来记住英文的发音了。",
    "traditional": "中國人這樣學英語\n\n    “託馬六、唵以、及夫、尤、唵五史為”，這是什麼意思？先別急，讀的時候想想英文。是的，這其實是“Tomorrow I give you answer”的發音。\n    這個是150年前英語書上的內容，是給中國人學英語用的。可能是因為那時候沒有錄音機，人們只能這樣來記住英文的發音了。"
  },
  "sentences": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "simplified": "\n\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "How the Chinese Study English"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "simplified": "“托马六、唵以、及夫、尤、唵五史为”，这是什么意思？",
      "traditional": "“託馬六、唵以、及夫、尤、唵五史為”，這是什麼意思？",
      "pinyin": "tuō mǎ liù ǎn yǐ jí fū yóu ǎn wǔ shǐ wèi zhè shì shén me yì si",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "simplified": "先别急，读的时候想想英文。",
      "traditional": "先別急，讀的時候想想英文。",
      "pinyin": "xiān bié jí dú de shí hou xiǎng xiǎng yīng wén",
      "english": "“Tuomaliu, anyi, jifu, you, anwushiwei”. What does this mean?"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "simplified": "是的，这其实是“Tomorrow I give you answer”的发音。",
      "traditional": "是的，這其實是“Tomorrow I give you answer”的發音。",
      "pinyin": "shì de zhè qí shí shì 1 1 1 1 1 de fā yīn",
      "english": "Calm down. Think in English when you read it."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "That's right, this is actually the pronunciation for “tomorrow I give you answer”."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "simplified": "这个是150年前英语书上的内容，是给中国人学英语用的。",
      "traditional": "這個是150年前英語書上的內容，是給中國人學英語用的。",
      "pinyin": "zhè ge shì 4 nián qián yīng yǔ shū shang de nèi róng shì gěi zhōng guó rén xué yīng yǔ yòng de",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "simplified": "可能是因为那时候没有录音机，人们只能这样来记住英文的发音了。",
      "traditional": "可能是因為那時候沒有錄音機，人們只能這樣來記住英文的發音了。",
      "pinyin": "kě néng shì yīn wèi nà shí hou méi yǒu lù yīn jī rén men zhǐ néng zhè yàng lái jì zhù yīng wén de fā yīn le",
      "english": "This is the content of a 150 year old English book, meant to be used by Chinese people to study English."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "simplified": "",
      "traditional": "",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Perhaps since there were no tape recorders at the time, people had to memorize English pronunciation like this."
    }
  ],
